{"tool_name":"soapsplice","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"soapsplice","version":"1.1","home":"http://soap.genomics.org.cn/soapsplice.html","license":"freely available","summary":"We have developed a tool SOAPsplice for genome-wide ab initio detection of splice junction sites from RNA-Seq, a method using new generation sequencing technologies to sequence the messenger RNA.","identifiers":["biotools:SOAPsplice","doi:10.3389/fgene.2011.00046"],"build":{"number":3,"skip":true},"requirements":{"build":null,"run":["zlib"]},"source_url":"https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/soapsplice/soapsplice_1.10_src_all.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["{ soapsplice || true; } | grep SOAPsplice"]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"soapsplice","identifiers":["biotools:SOAPsplice","doi:10.3389/fgene.2011.00046","doi:10.1038/nmeth.4106"],"license":"freely available","summary":"We have developed a tool soapsplice for genome-wide ab initio detection of splice junction sites from rna-seq, a method using new generation sequencing technologies to sequence the messenger rna.","home_url":"http://soap.genomics.org.cn/soapsplice.html","keywords":["Benchmarking","Computer Simulation","Exons","Genome, Human","Humans","Introns","Molecular Sequence Annotation","Plasmodium falciparum","Polymorphism, Genetic","RNA Splicing","Sequence Alignment","Sequence Analysis, RNA","RNA splicing"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"soapsplice","home":"http://soap.genomics.org.cn/index.html","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Designed to use RNA-Seq reads for genome-wide ab initio detection of splice junction sites and identification of alternative splicing (AS) events.","addition_date":"2017-08-20T17:29:09Z","last_update_date":"2019-09-04T08:38:37Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Animal and Crop Genomics"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:soapsplice","credit":[{"email":"pengbgi@gmail.com","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://soap.genomics.org.cn/soapsplice.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["animalandcropgenomics"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Splice site prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0433"}]}],"name":"SOAPsplice","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"admin","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nmeth.4106","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 Nature America, inc., part of springer Nature. All rights reserved.Alignment is the first step in most RNA-seq analysis pipelines, and the accuracy of downstream analyses depends heavily on it. Unlike most steps in the pipeline, alignment is particularly amenable to benchmarking with simulated data. We performed a comprehensive benchmarking of 14 common splice-aware aligners for base, read, and exon junction-level accuracy and compared default with optimized parameters. We found that performance varied by genome complexity, and accuracy and popularity were poorly correlated. The most widely cited tool underperforms for most metrics, particularly when using default settings.","authors":[{"name":"Baruzzo G."},{"name":"DI Camillo B."},{"name":"Fitzgerald G.A."},{"name":"Grant G.R."},{"name":"Hayer K.E."},{"name":"Kim E.J."}],"citationCount":114,"date":"2017-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Simulation-based comprehensive benchmarking of RNA-seq aligners"},"pmcid":"PMC5792058","pmid":"27941783","type":["Benchmarking study"]},{"doi":"10.3389/fgene.2011.00046","metadata":{"abstract":"RNA-Seq, a method using next generation sequencing technologies to sequence the tran-scriptome, facilitates genome-wide analysis of splice junction sites. In this paper, we introduce SOAPsplice, a robust tool to detect splice junctions using RNA-Seq data without using any information of known splice junctions. SOAPsplice uses a novel two-step approach consisting of first identifying as many reasonable splice junction candidates as possible, and then, filtering the false positives with two effective filtering strategies. In both simulated and real datasets, SOAPsplice is able to detect many reliable splice junctions with low false positive rate. The improvement gained by SOAPsplice, when compared to other existing tools, becomes more obvious when the depth of sequencing is low. SOAPsplice is freely available at http://soap.genomics.org.cn/soapsplice.html. \u00a9 2011 Huang, Zhang, Li, Zhang He, Lam, Peng and Yiu.","authors":[{"name":"He Z."},{"name":"Huang S."},{"name":"Lam T.-W."},{"name":"Li R."},{"name":"Peng Z."},{"name":"Yiu S.-M."},{"name":"Zhang J."},{"name":"Zhang W."}],"citationCount":79,"date":"2011-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Frontiers in Genetics","title":"SOAPsplice: Genome-wide ab initio detection of splice junctions from RNA-Seq data"},"pmcid":"PMC3268599","pmid":"22303342","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA splicing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3320"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SOAPsplice","home":"https://bio.tools/soapsplice","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Designed to use RNA-Seq reads for genome-wide ab initio detection of splice junction sites and identification of alternative splicing (AS) events.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:soapsplice/cmd/soap.genomics.org.cn","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":51,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":1,"year":"2025"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":2,"year":"2017"},{"count":3,"year":"2018"},{"count":3,"year":"2021"},{"count":4,"year":"2019"},{"count":5,"year":"2013"},{"count":5,"year":"2015"},{"count":12,"year":"201